# Where the Django API lives. Read at build time by src/proxy.ts to build the
# CSP connect-src and img-src, and at runtime by src/lib/api.ts.
#
# Get this wrong and the browser blocks every request the console makes: the
# screens render, the data never arrives, and the console log fills with CSP
# violations. It is the first thing to check when nothing loads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ---- Media base URL ----
# Where product and category images are read from. OPTIONAL, and unset it falls
# back to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — which is correct while the backend runs
# UPLOAD_BACKEND=local and Django serves /uploads itself.
#
# Set it once images live in Cloudflare R2: the bucket's public base, either its
# r2.dev subdomain or a custom domain. The backend calls the same value
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL, and the two must agree — the API stores relative paths
# ("/uploads/x.png") and this is what puts a host in front of them.
#
# Read at build time by src/proxy.ts to name the origin in the CSP's `img-src`,
# so a wrong value means the browser blocks every product image with nothing in
# any server log. Changing it needs a rebuild, not a restart.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_URL=https://pub-<32 hex>.r2.dev
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_URL=https://cdn.edawr.in
